"""Synchronous SOSIX secure staging-directory operation.

Thin facades over the runtime-owned split crossing (runtime_native.c
rt_secure_temp_dir_set_parent / _set_prefix / _make, with interpreter twins):
set the parent, set the leaf prefix, then make consumes both thread-local
slots and returns the new 0700 directory path, or an empty/nil text on any
failure. Set calls return 1 when the slot was filled. Every text argument
must be a heap text (a string literal crosses the text ABI as (NULL, len));
`file_ops.secure_temp_dir_raw` is the composed caller. These are the only
declarations of the three externs.

Facades rather than `export use ... as` renames: the seed interpreter cannot
resolve an aliased extern import
(doc/08_tracking/bug/seed_interpreter_aliased_extern_import_not_found_2026_10_19.md).
"""

@unsafe(reason: "stores the staging parent in a thread-local slot for the paired make call", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_secure_temp_dir_set_parent(parent: text) -> i64
@unsafe(reason: "stores the staging leaf prefix in a thread-local slot for the paired make call", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_secure_temp_dir_set_prefix(prefix: text) -> i64
@unsafe(reason: "creates the OS-owned private staging directory from the slotted parent and prefix", capabilities: [ffi])
extern fn rt_secure_temp_dir_make() -> text

@always_inline
pub fn sosix_secure_temp_dir_set_parent(parent: text) -> i64:
    unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]):
        rt_secure_temp_dir_set_parent(parent)

@always_inline
pub fn sosix_secure_temp_dir_set_prefix(prefix: text) -> i64:
    unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]):
        rt_secure_temp_dir_set_prefix(prefix)

@always_inline
pub fn sosix_secure_temp_dir_make() -> text:
    unsafe(capabilities: [ffi]):
        rt_secure_temp_dir_make()
